md+='\nThe compressed embedded files are audit reference snapshots under their own notices, not a production mapping license grant. Do not publish STEP/SWORD-derived app mapping data from this audit. No correspondence from the printed concordance is encoded by this script.\n';
section('3. Per-book coverage');
md+='\n### SWORD LXX versus Vulg actual registrations\n\n```text\n'+swordInventory.LXX.registration+'\n'+swordInventory.Vulg.registration+'\n```\n\nLXX registers verse limits without a mapping array; Vulg registers mappings_vulg. Vulg includes '+swordInventory.Vulg.rows+' encoded rule rows, including separate-book routing for EpJer/PrAzar/Sus/Bel. Those describe Vulg↔KJVA behavior, not an LXX→Vulg bridge. The missing LXX edge prevents applying them to Swete without guessing; zero evaluated edges below means unavailable, not no counterpart. The Vulg header explicitly describes a compromise across editions, not Nova Vulgata or WEB-C.\n';
table(['Vulg book (external name)','Source book number in table','Explicit encoded rules','Swete applicability'],swordInventory.Vulg.bookRows.map(b=>[b.name,b.sourceBookNumber,b.explicitRows,'No cited LXX→Vulg edge']));
md+='\n### Printed concordance — human check only\n\nThe fetched CCEL page reproduces a revised Brenton table and a separate list explicitly labeled “Swete p. 233”. Its columns distinguish Rahlfs/CATSS and Brenton, and the lower Swete list differs at several chapter divisions and subdivided clauses. It therefore reinforces the edition-specific blocker. No row from this printed-table transcription is expanded or used as machine correspondence by the script. Exact URL/date/hash is in the source inventory.\n';
for(const c of candidates.filter(c=>!c.id.endsWith('defaults'))){md+='\n### '+c.id+' — '+c.status+'\n\n';table(['Canon book','Has raw Swete content?','Explicit source mapping clauses','Coverage judgment'],canon.map(b=>{const aliases=b.id==='EST'?['ESG','EST']:b.id==='DAN'?['DAG','DAN','SUS','BEL']:b.id==='BAR'?['BAR','LJE']:b.id==='NEH'?['EZR']: [b.id];const raw=books.some(x=>x.label===b.id||(b.id==='EZR'||b.id==='NEH')&&x.label==='EZR+NEH');const clauses=c.source.rows.filter(r=>aliases.some(id=>(r.left??'').toUpperCase().startsWith(id)));return [b.id,raw?'present':b.id==='ECC'?'ABSENT upstream':'absent (NT outside LXX scope)',clauses.length,!raw?'not applicable':clauses.length?'PARTIAL explicit instructions; WEB-C bridge not proved':c.source.declared.has(aliases[0])?'identity default only; NOT explicit correspondence':'no explicit map'];}));}
md+='\nKingdoms aliases are explicitly described in SIL lxx.vrs comments: 1SA/2SA = Orthodox 1/2 Kings, 1KI/2KI = Orthodox 3/4 Kings. Combined Esdras B corresponds to EZR in that file; EZR 11-23 → NEH is supplied by cited clauses, not an assumed -10 offset. Psalm superscriptions must retain 0, numbered title, and detached title distinctions. PRO has limits but no explicit rearrangement clauses in SIL/CA; native 29 chapters cannot be assumed aligned to a 31-chapter target. Daniel/Baruch components require explicit routes; namespaces alone cannot prove them. Esther prologue has no automatically invented numbered placement.\n';
section('4. Actual source application: reference predictions, not validated alignments');table(['Candidate','Witness','Source records','Map to ≥1 canon slot','No canon slot','Multiple canon slots','Unresolved (no supported rule)','Explicit no counterpart','Canon slots without source (73 books)','OT slots without source','Outside target edges'],report.applications.map(a=>[a.id,a.witness,a.total,a.mapped,a.noCanon,a.multiple,a.unresolved,a.explicitNone,a.canonWithoutSource,a.otWithoutSource,a.outside.length]));
md+='\nUnresolved does NOT mean Scripture has no counterpart. Explicit no-counterpart requires an external source instruction, never a failed lookup. Out-of-range checks are mechanical sanity checks only. Default-mode figures are predictions under a generic English scheme and include known semantic failures; no approval is implied by high coverage. Empty raw source containers are counted without adding text.\n';
for(const a of report.applications){md+='\n### '+a.id+' '+a.witness+' — ALL outside targets\n\n';table(['Source','Candidate source ref','Target','Provenance'],a.outside.map(o=>[o.source,o.sourceRef??'',o.target,JSON.stringify(o.provenance)]));if(a.excludedPresent.length){md+='\nSource records that the candidate declares excluded (retain raw content):\n';table(['Source','Ref','Raw text'],a.excludedPresent.map(r=>[r.key,r.ref,r.text]));}}
