section('5. Daniel witness: actual boundaries only');table(['WEB-C ref','Actual WEB-C text'],webBoundaries.filter(x=>x.ref.startsWith('DAN')).map(r=>[r.ref,r.text]));for(const w of witnesses){md+='\n### '+w.file+'\n\n'+w.url+'\n\n';table(['Swete source ref','Actual raw boundary text'],w.boundaryRows.map(r=>[r.ref,r.text]));}
md+='\nObserved boundary conclusion: WEB-C follows the Theodotion-associated arrangement at the inspected boundaries: 3:23 the bound men fall in, 3:24 walking/praising, 3:25 Azarias begins prayer; the three-voice hymn begins 3:51 with blessings at 3:52, deliverance resumes 3:91, and promotion occurs 3:97. Old Greek has a different 3:24 introductory sentence. Susanna closes with Daniel becoming great (WEB 13:64, Theodotion Sus 1:64); Old Greek instead ends with 62a/62b moralizing material. Bel begins with Astyages/Cyrus (WEB 14:1, Theodotion 1:1); Old Greek begins with a Habakkuk attribution. This is boundary evidence, not a statement about translation quality or every verse. Neither Swete witness is arranged as WEB-C chapters 13/14: components are separate. Both Swete Daniel chapter 3 witnesses retain 3:98-100 where WEB-C moves the royal proclamation to 4:1-3. The cached Theodotion Bel file stops mid-sentence at 1:36: WEB 14:41-42 cannot be checked against that source. Do not reconstruct it from Old Greek.\n';
section('Independent WEB-C target checks');table(['WEB-C ref','Actual target text'],webBoundaries.filter(x=>x.ref.startsWith('BAR')).map(r=>[r.ref,r.text]));
md+='\nLetter of Jeremiah source verse 1 begins the captivity warning, whereas WEB BAR 6:1 is the prose letter introduction and BAR 6:2 begins the captivity warning. Generic eng.vrs predicts source 1 → BAR 6:1; STEP Greek also predicts BAR 6:1. These predictions fail this boundary check. At the end, generic eng.vrs predicts LJE 1:72 → BAR 6:72; STEP Greek predicts BAR 6:73. The actual closing maxim occurs in source verse 72 and WEB 6:73. These observations do NOT authorize a hand-written correction: no audited external full WEB-C bridge was found. The Swete prose introduction is detached body text and must not be assigned a source verse without a cited policy.\n';
md+='\nPsalms: generic eng.vrs targets numeric verse 0 for titles; canon has no 0 slot. LXX 9:22 has overlapping original-scheme clauses (10:0 and 10:1), retained as a conflict rather than silently overwritten. Exact predicted splits are printed above from external rows. Jeremiah 25:14 predictions differ among Greek traditions and source metadata; equal chapter totals are irrelevant. Esther expanded English ESG numbering is not WEB-C EST numbering: several predicted addition targets exceed actual canon limits. SIL and Copenhagen share ancestry, so their agreement is not independent evidence.\n';
section('6. Proposed smallest static shape — DESIGN ONLY');
md+='\n```js\nwindow.MARANATHA_LXX_MAPPING = {\n  scheme: "<approved Swete-to-WEB-C scheme id>",\n  sourceCommit: "<pinned Swete commit>",\n  targetCanonSHA256: "<canon hash>",\n  provenance: [/* { url, commit, sha256, license } */],\n  entries: {\n    "<Swete witness/book/chapter/verse>": {\n      to: [/* canon references; [] ONLY for externally attested no counterpart */],\n      p: [/* [provenanceIndex, external line or JSON pointer] per entry */]\n    }\n  }\n};\n```\n\nAn absent entry means unresolved, never identity or no counterpart. Retain separate witness IDs, segment suffixes, zero/title references and original text; to may have multiple destinations without splitting or rewriting text. This is a symbolic schema, not real mapping entries. Load through a script tag; no local fetch(). Runtime adapter would index cited source refs per canon cell while preserving text and source citation. Covered book with no mapped verse can use existing missing-verse state; absent source book uses missing-book. Unresolved mapping must carry a distinct explanation and remain outside aligned rows, rather than claiming textual absence. Existing separate versification display can carry native unresolved passages. Inspect VerseAvailability states before implementation; do not silently concatenate or duplicate Scripture when multiple sources feed one cell.\n\nvalidate.mjs would need an optional mapping-aware path: validate source refs against the exact native witness corpus, destination refs against canon, provenance and licenses for every entry, explicit [] versus unknown, all multiplicities and collisions, exclusions and unmapped coverage, witness consistency, canon/source hashes, and semantic regression anchors. Source-native chapter/verse counts must not be compared directly to canon counts as alignment validation. Retain current validation for existing translations. Provisional canon entries are not permission to hide out-of-range mappings. All changes remain design only.\n';
section('Local input hashes');table(['Read-only local input','SHA256'],localFiles.map(x=>[x.file,x.sha256]));
section('RECOMMENDATION');md+='\nNo evaluated source is a complete verified Swete → current WEB-C canon mapping. Use licensed Copenhagen/Paratext data as a starting reference, not a ready importer table. SIL and Copenhagen are alternatives with shared ancestry; combining them is not independent corroboration. A future hybrid may be needed for edition-specific Swete references and WEB-C additions/title conventions, but every extra edge must come from a separately cited licensed source. STEP is a rich cross-check candidate with conditional Greek alternatives; its conflicting redistribution wording must be clarified before shipping data derived from it. SWORD Vulg cannot fill the missing SWORD LXX correspondence edge.\n';
section('BLOCKERS');md+='\n- Establish a licensed, external WEB-C-specific bridge; generic English, Vulgate, Original and Greek schemes are not interchangeable.\n- Resolve externally, not by local fixes: Letter introduction/offset, Esther addition references, native Proverbs ordering and superscriptions.\n- Obtain independent passage-level evidence for Jeremiah order and the Greek tradition used by each Swete book; retain candidate disagreements.\n- Decide Daniel witness and separate-component placement with cited edges; incomplete Theodotion Bel remains a raw-source gap.\n- Clarify STEP redistribution grant and GPL restrictions before using either for app data.\n- Preserve explicit unknown versus no counterpart and multiplicity; verify body titles/introductions without inventing source references.\n- User approval is required before any importer, mapping dataset or application/validator changes. STOP after audit.\n';
